# E §5 step 3 (tally 2.1.2, issue #34, the hole-when sibling in the user's ruling): E5_adjust_hole_when_later's twin.
# late (known 2026-05-01) makes rent[2026-03]'s when a hole; ended (known 2026-07-01) makes it false, ending the
# instance, measured against the hole state: δ = −A_previous, a hole. Two hole adjustments (n), both unsettled, so the
# reads reaching 2026-07-01 hold both HOLE-CHANGED questions (q). tally 2.1.1's refcore
# skipped late's step and measured ended's against the booking: one adjustment of 500.00 PLN dated 2026-07-01.
=== m.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source plan "plan"
source act "act"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place landlord: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input total: money PLN
input tenants[m in months]: int
input dom: int
input seats[m in months]: int

move rent[m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, dom)
  at start_of(m)
  when seats[m] > 0
  leg cash from konto to landlord amount round(total / tenants[m], minor(PLN), half-even)

version plan_2026
  cite plan
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  total = 1 000.00 PLN "umowa"
  dom = 10 "umowa"
  tenants[*] = 2 "umowa"
  seats[*] = 1 "umowa"
  opening[konto] = 10 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"

version late
  cite act
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-05-01
  replace seats[*] = ?"how many seats in March?" "aneks"

version ended
  cite act
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-07-01
  replace seats[*] = 0 "aneks 2"

ask n: count(x in adjustments over 2026)
ask q: flows(rent, 2026-07-01 .. 2026-07-31)
=== expect
n: 2
  cut 2026-10-20
q: ?"rent[2026-03] on 2026-03-10 changed after it was paid (version ended); is back pay due, and when?" (rent[2026-03]) ?"rent[2026-03] on 2026-03-10 changed after it was paid (version late); is back pay due, and when?" (rent[2026-03])
  unfulfilled: rent[2026-07]
  cut 2026-10-20
